A node that cannot be reached does not automatically have configuration drift.

## 120. The Investigation Quality Scorecard

Evaluate the quality of completed investigations using explicit dimensions:

- Evidence coverage.
- Freshness.
- Independent corroboration.
- Hypothesis discrimination.
- Verification completeness.
- Contradiction resolution.
- Operational safety.
- Human review status.
- Outcome confirmation.

Do not convert this into a fake universal probability of correctness.

Show the constituent dimensions and how the system calculated them.

Where scores are heuristic, say so.

Use the scorecard to identify process improvements, not to reward superficial certainty.

